## Model tiers

`/plan` writes a `## Parallel execution map` (shards with a `tier`) and
`/build` fans the shards out to workers. Pick the model by role:

| Role | Tier | Cursor `model:` | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Planner, technical reviewer, integrator | high-reasoning | inherit (parent chat) | Use a high-reasoning chat model for `/plan` |
| Review agents (Phase 3, plan review) | pinned | as pinned in each agent file | Never override on `Task` |
| `reasoning` shard worker | high-reasoning | inherit | Rare; most shards are `code` |
| `code` shard worker | fast coding | `composer-2.5` | Default for fan-out |
| `mechanical` shard worker | cheapest | `composer-2.5` or `gpt-5.6-luna-fast` | See slug note |

Slug status: `composer-2.5` is confirmed in the Task tool's model list.
`gpt-5.6-luna-fast`, `claude-opus-5-5`, and `gpt-5.6-sol` were reported
available on 2026-09-22 but are **unverified** in the current schema —
confirm with `agent --list-models` (or the chat model picker) before
pinning. If a slug is rejected, fall back to `composer-2.5` or omit
`model` to inherit. The user may override any tier; honour
`> Model override:` lines under the plan's map.

Shard workers are generic executors, not review agents:

```text
Task({
  subagent_type: "generalPurpose",
  description: "Shard <id>",
  model: "composer-2.5",
  run_in_background: true,
  prompt: "<worker prompt template from the build skill>"
})
```

## Rolling-window fan-out

`/build` parallel mode keeps up to `maxParallel` workers running: launch
every ready shard in **one** turn, and as soon as any worker returns,
launch the shards it unblocked while the rest keep running. Practical
ceiling is about 12 concurrent Tasks; dozens overwhelm the host.

Anti-patterns:

- **Batch-and-wait** — launching a batch, then idling until every worker
  in it returns before launching the next batch
- **Serial shards** — one worker at a time on a plan that has a map
- **One giant worker** — a single Task owning most of the shard paths
- Workers editing `sharedFiles`, pushing, or switching branches
- Overriding a review agent's pinned model on `Task`
- Launching workers before validating the map (overlaps, cycles)

## Tool scoping

- `flutter-reviewer` has `readonly: true` — no file edits
- Other reviewers must write raw reports under `docs/reviews/raw/`
- Never pass `readonly` as a Task argument (agent-file field only)

## Anti-patterns

- Narrating "I'll invoke the vgv-review-agent" without a Task call
- Wrong type strings (`vgv-review`, `VGVReviewAgent`, `@vgv-review-agent`)
- Sequential Phase 3 reviews when skill says parallel
- Relative `docs/reviews/raw` without `$PWD` prefix in subagent prompt
- Falling back to `generalPurpose` before install + Cursor restart

